# Line endings are normalised in the repository and in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# Two reasons, neither of them cosmetic:
#
# - `packages/create/templates/**` ships verbatim in the published tarball — `write.ts` writes the bytes it
#   read, and `files` carries the directory as-is. So the templates' line endings are whichever the
#   publishing checkout had. A release cut from a checkout with `core.autocrlf` on would hand every scaffolded
#   app CRLF files; Prettier's `--check` ignores line endings, so nothing would fail, but the first
#   `pnpm format` would rewrite every file in the project. The generator should not produce a different
#   project depending on which machine published it.
#
# - The suites read templates and fixtures off disk and compare what they find. A Windows checkout used to
#   hand the scaffolder's own suite `dist/\r` where it expected `dist/`, which failed on windows-latest only
#   — the least useful place to find out. Two neighbouring assertions survived the same conversion by
#   accident, through a `trimEnd()` and a CRLF-to-CRLF comparison.
#
# Safe to apply wholesale: nothing tracked here is binary, and there is no `.bat`, `.cmd` or `.ps1` that
# needs CRLF. `text=auto` would leave a binary file alone regardless.
* text=auto eol=lf
